.TH UUDECODE 1.SH NAMEuuencode, uudecode \- encode a binary file as text, and back.SH SYNOPSIS\fBuuencode\fRinfile > outfile.br\fBuudecode\fR[infile].SH DESCRIPTION\fBuuencode\fRwrites a file as printable text, safe to send through mail: a\fBbegin\fRline with the mode and the name, the data four bytes to three inprintable characters, and an\fBend\fRline.  Give it the one file and redirect its output:\fBuuencode notes > notes.uu\fR.\fRIts usage line reads as though it wants a name as well, and given twoarguments it prints that line and stops..PP\fBuudecode\fRreads such text, from the file named or the standard input, and writesthe original into the current directory under the name on its\fBbegin\fRline..SH NOTESBoth need Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOmimecode, btoa